WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.701
-You know, lately
I have been having a great time

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:03.736
watching old movies.
I especially like watching them

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:06.071
on the Cherished Cinema Classics
channel.

00:00:06.071 --> 00:00:07.740
The host is super knowledgeable

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.109
and gives really interesting
introductions to the films.

00:00:10.109 --> 00:00:11.377
Check this out.

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:18.651 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:21.387
-Welcome back to
Cherished Cinema Classics.

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:23.523 line:0%
I'm your host, Clyde Darwell.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:27.526 line:0%
Next up, from 1946,
"Passion on the Prairie."

00:00:27.526 --> 00:00:30.964
A thrilling frontier romance
starring Van Westmore,

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:33.799
Constance Pigeon,
and Everett Zuker.

00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:36.035
Though a huge box office success
in its day,

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:39.138
it's worth noting this film
is a product of its time.

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:41.140
By today's standards,
it contains

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.977
outdated insensitive portrayals
of African-Americans.

00:00:44.977 --> 00:00:47.380
But keeping that in mind,
we hope you can look past

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.783
those flaws and enjoy
this American classic,

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:53.853
which I should also note is
offensive to Native Americans,

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:56.022
Asian Americans,
Lebanese Americans,

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:58.691
the Inuit,
and Estonian Americans.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:00.159
But having said that,

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:03.429
it's a vital piece of film
history that is to be treasured.

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:05.598
So, sit back, relax,

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:09.535
and also a quick note about
the love scenes in this film.

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:15.141
They don't all seem entirely,
how you say, consensual.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:18.811
Grabbing women and kissing them
by force, and when they resist,

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:21.881
slapping them was considered
romantic in the 1940s.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.516
Now, not so much.

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:26.218
Nevertheless, this movie
remains a pinnacle

00:01:26.218 --> 00:01:27.954
of Hollywood's Golden Age.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:30.389
So pour yourself a tall soda
and settle in

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:32.458
for the splendid
three-hour spectacle,

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:34.760
"Passion on the Prairie."

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:40.632 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:40.632 --> 00:01:42.001
Wait, one more thing.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.871
I should warn viewers sensitive
to this sort of thing,

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:48.340
there's a graphic whale hunt
midway through the film.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:53.313
Also what some might consider
gratuitous kicking of a beagle.

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:56.415
Anyway, I think
that covers it all.

00:01:56.415 --> 00:02:00.253
African-Americans,
beagle kick, consent.

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:01.521
Yeah, that's it.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:05.458
Now let's travel back to 1946
with the historic,

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:07.893
incomparable
Cherished Cinema Classic

00:02:07.893 --> 00:02:10.363
"Passion on the Prairie."

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:14.467 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.769
Oh, wait, I forgot a biggie.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.505
This movie is
super sympathetic to Nazis,

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:22.508
which seems really late
for 1946.

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:23.776
So, here we go.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:26.112
Wait.
There's also a scene

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:29.381
where a non-binary ranch hand
is referred to by

00:02:29.381 --> 00:02:30.917
the improper pronoun,

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:34.020
which actually seems way ahead
of its time.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.421
You know what?

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.256
Let's cut out
the problematic scenes

00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:40.392
and show only parts of the movie
that aren't offensive now.

00:02:40.392 --> 00:02:42.027
Does that sound good?

00:02:42.027 --> 00:02:43.529
"Passion on the Prairie."

00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:44.997
Roll it.

00:02:44.997 --> 00:02:53.406 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:56.376
Wow. They don't make 'em
like that anymore.

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:58.811
Next up on
Cherished Cinema Classics,

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:01.514
the 1932 screwball
comedy classic

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.616
"Real Men Don't Wear Skirts."

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.918
Oh, brother. Here we go again.

00:03:05.918 --> 00:03:12.858 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:12.858 --> 00:03:14.227
-Yeah, they're gonna have
a rough season.

